{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:34:00Z","created_by_operation":"op_622df7aed7584006b02a904d5b42cb09","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_087625134d58de08f29b7d6db36d59d42238b63c6209f66d7963572e6ca75ff6","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=dependencies","setting":"qwenlm/qwen-code@7e0beb9d1823 snapshot 0429dc14353565eb","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_020698bbf964dbd2b4da9a1f94857c279cdfa6eef68bcdbf034c06c10e8c139a","slc_23b4d2b2ec23d72e847ead2d641fe968e3b549068912a8eaaa45259b9087a5c7","slc_a7081fa328637e98ddeacff589a30720aa949cb849978a5614504ee83fcefd8b"],"source_ids":["src_0223cfa9e0ba5300ab46d42e77375e48"],"text":"NPM installation requires Node.js 22+; the project was originally based on Google Gemini CLI v0.8.2 but stopped syncing upstream starting from Qwen Code v0.1.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:34:00Z","updated_by_operation":"op_622df7aed7584006b02a904d5b42cb09"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:34:00Z","created_by_operation":"op_622df7aed7584006b02a904d5b42cb09","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_08d2e35bb045bb91e815fa67d94fae91be0691738d13f973553a59e88ddd6232","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"qwenlm/qwen-code@7e0beb9d1823 snapshot 0429dc14353565eb","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_81761c39ba4b6d215f182dba35262bcb263d5dbf0da98ff353424e54faaed6e2"],"source_ids":["src_d7eeff27735e54acaabd783ed77d565f"],"text":"In daemon mode with multi-workspace sessions, each live workspace runtime owns its own bridge and `qwen --acp` child, with filesystem access, environment overlays, MCP transports, and sessions scoped to that runtime.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:34:00Z","updated_by_operation":"op_622df7aed7584006b02a904d5b42cb09"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:34:00Z","created_by_operation":"op_622df7aed7584006b02a904d5b42cb09","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_110a3814d4d12db7b301a02be5711930193930f1730ac15a4b35f6e90ddcae23","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=workflows","setting":"qwenlm/qwen-code@7e0beb9d1823 snapshot 0429dc14353565eb","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_f84a414bfc2bd9074b24d28926f9c54b3997d829d78ccf988a067f411782076e"],"source_ids":["src_0223cfa9e0ba5300ab46d42e77375e48"],"text":"Repository development practice: contributions are directed to CONTRIBUTING.md for guidelines.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:34:00Z","updated_by_operation":"op_622df7aed7584006b02a904d5b42cb09"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:34:00Z","created_by_operation":"op_622df7aed7584006b02a904d5b42cb09","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_254bea1c00a829fc129a389f13de362f4c10ee854fbfdd18b64958c24034b408","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"qwenlm/qwen-code@7e0beb9d1823 snapshot 0429dc14353565eb","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_9aff7da9a99737baacf1cdd15de6805ef2db3a8db9b26a58d6c8083747803362","slc_b08d3a38753888d5afb2f2232c1d001e358506a5396930a19bd963d3e9415741","slc_e35d897f6ddbc0b96063f90f239b0110d3ef925bc39292a1f49a8b9a253878fd"],"source_ids":["src_0223cfa9e0ba5300ab46d42e77375e48","src_d7eeff27735e54acaabd783ed77d565f"],"text":"The product offers multiple invocation surfaces: an interactive `qwen` TUI started in a project directory, headless `qwen -p \"...\"` for scripts/CI, and an experimental `qwen serve` daemon exposing HTTP + SSE (ACP).","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:34:00Z","updated_by_operation":"op_622df7aed7584006b02a904d5b42cb09"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:34:00Z","created_by_operation":"op_622df7aed7584006b02a904d5b42cb09","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_39be8499f6049f7de9d74a1031bfb54c3919074de076ba21029a6c507251d9ff","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"qwenlm/qwen-code@7e0beb9d1823 snapshot 0429dc14353565eb","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_10222c4ab9e4c8088d6acd61d8be0444b5be6f8b471fea04ac3773beecbff756","slc_eeb5aefce36b903e1785393cc267583829a7c5c3b5a33f0850bb42f3cc3f69cd"],"source_ids":["src_d7eeff27735e54acaabd783ed77d565f"],"text":"The core runtime owns the agent loop — model requests, conversation context, tool dispatch, permission policy — while display and transport decisions are deliberately kept in the CLI, bridge, SDK, and UI layers.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:34:00Z","updated_by_operation":"op_622df7aed7584006b02a904d5b42cb09"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:34:00Z","created_by_operation":"op_622df7aed7584006b02a904d5b42cb09","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_5e578832269ca9d7a4f80cefa8da12ade2d771e104b97f986b1ab9a323cbda68","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"qwenlm/qwen-code@7e0beb9d1823 snapshot 0429dc14353565eb","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_9aff7da9a99737baacf1cdd15de6805ef2db3a8db9b26a58d6c8083747803362","slc_c10f885ab0f5b3547927e6c8f0db3106e47f58909d2a5f190182c751349d2963"],"source_ids":["src_0223cfa9e0ba5300ab46d42e77375e48"],"text":"Inside a session, `/auth` configures the provider and API key; the CLI is started by running `qwen` in a project directory.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:34:00Z","updated_by_operation":"op_622df7aed7584006b02a904d5b42cb09"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:34:00Z","created_by_operation":"op_622df7aed7584006b02a904d5b42cb09","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_8e0cb7db4b61a63442af47fb149dede015d4c3bfecf21cc08189cabeb5a57040","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"qwenlm/qwen-code@7e0beb9d1823 snapshot 0429dc14353565eb","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_b485e05a89c15ab4b8b018771513f15993fe425bcd6743fa602282b6fe6dab72"],"source_ids":["src_0223cfa9e0ba5300ab46d42e77375e48"],"text":"The agent supports multiple model protocols — OpenAI, Anthropic, Gemini, and Qwen APIs — plus third-party or local providers (Ollama/vLLM), switchable at runtime.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:34:00Z","updated_by_operation":"op_622df7aed7584006b02a904d5b42cb09"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:34:00Z","created_by_operation":"op_622df7aed7584006b02a904d5b42cb09","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_99f38ef03d95427a3ef5cbefaf52bf96b869e3dbe35dea01b1159a008c70eab8","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"qwenlm/qwen-code@7e0beb9d1823 snapshot 0429dc14353565eb","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_21380e9ddad84a224ad2d48a60ed8863c03647070142e0282d2ec4a382b9cddb","slc_35da8b11939860901c47889de3ce858fe19c62ae7a781502be4b5743022ed4bf","slc_bcb582d24d78a0871c6aecdca091584f6cd7f49b7436f23ff6d7ed8f6dbae27e"],"source_ids":["src_3987d8bc94a15f189c12bede1626f7e0"],"text":"A daemon side-channel coordination design doc specifies that in-session model changes are demuxed from `extNotification()` while approval-mode changes use the ACP `current_mode_update` sessionUpdate, since no `current_model_update` ACP type exists.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:34:00Z","updated_by_operation":"op_622df7aed7584006b02a904d5b42cb09"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:34:00Z","created_by_operation":"op_622df7aed7584006b02a904d5b42cb09","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_ba678e712368f880bc4037da02af772d1e5c5aab114626cc48b30580e2e968fd","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=components","setting":"qwenlm/qwen-code@7e0beb9d1823 snapshot 0429dc14353565eb","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_cee93e1b0ef189f31c9e79be1e5b96a3d94699dc31958ff05e0da50511c8ee2f"],"source_ids":["src_d7eeff27735e54acaabd783ed77d565f"],"text":"Key monorepo packages: `packages/cli` (executable, arg parsing, Ink TUI, headless output, ACP entry, `qwen serve`), `packages/core` (agent orchestration, tools, permissions, sessions, memory), and `packages/acp-bridge` (ACP channel lifecycle, session multiplexing, permission mediation).","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:34:00Z","updated_by_operation":"op_622df7aed7584006b02a904d5b42cb09"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:34:00Z","created_by_operation":"op_622df7aed7584006b02a904d5b42cb09","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_cda91ac3d6e68c0fe48d71a3c99e331cf3416a0f6c067eb357cdfd29248ae0c2","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=evaluation","setting":"qwenlm/qwen-code@7e0beb9d1823 snapshot 0429dc14353565eb","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_c6e531e262b0dae1b6c3b3f6c0873591a5af700930394e544b8fb3376557e460","slc_fa3ba3f60732fd6af77c5b91db580f4125ab399ec21fcdb6903359bb0695fdd6"],"source_ids":["src_0223cfa9e0ba5300ab46d42e77375e48"],"text":"The README reports a SWE-bench Verified evaluation (500 cases, 3 trials per version, model Qwen 3.7 Max) with average scores between roughly 76.4% and 77.8% across seven Qwen Code versions.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:34:00Z","updated_by_operation":"op_622df7aed7584006b02a904d5b42cb09"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:34:00Z","created_by_operation":"op_622df7aed7584006b02a904d5b42cb09","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_d93e84acb57184c6b602b37a0466ed377676b55cf30dc20766760a81754e90d4","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=relevance","setting":"qwenlm/qwen-code@7e0beb9d1823 snapshot 0429dc14353565eb","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_3c2922ee503097d0b2cb76f608b44faaa2367919ba99a9b75815fa75cbc2b950","slc_b70135d777f5ce7054e4e2b801a23c66c5768cafce3aa4a7754ae3bed239d841","slc_dcad4ae28a128b953bf811814d18b7d426b99994893abfea994bde88e594e344"],"source_ids":["src_0223cfa9e0ba5300ab46d42e77375e48"],"text":"Qwen Code is positioned as an open-source AI coding agent for terminal, editor, desktop, browser, and chat, aiming for feature parity with Claude Code plus multi-protocol and daemon-mode extras.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:34:00Z","updated_by_operation":"op_622df7aed7584006b02a904d5b42cb09"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:34:00Z","created_by_operation":"op_622df7aed7584006b02a904d5b42cb09","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_ea38d7ebb4fdafa5771e94f673c8eb20e4362289e183ac1bb1dd18d6796e71de","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"qwenlm/qwen-code@7e0beb9d1823 snapshot 0429dc14353565eb","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_14fcb3076f5c7f822c19826db246ade7bbfe839191a41d0be483b11539db4cdc","slc_a9839df6edc826248331356efa992ae148f592a04977e6165e61cc5f0be72fa5","slc_bf2f06486eb10835c6ea291f893795116748bd3fd84ab00d943da6cbb923b724","slc_e35d897f6ddbc0b96063f90f239b0110d3ef925bc39292a1f49a8b9a253878fd"],"source_ids":["src_0223cfa9e0ba5300ab46d42e77375e48"],"text":"SDKs exist for TypeScript, Python, and Java; the Python SDK exposes an async `query()` taking a cwd and path to the qwen executable, streaming messages from which result messages are printed.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:34:00Z","updated_by_operation":"op_622df7aed7584006b02a904d5b42cb09"}
